# Project Stack & Commands

## Stack

- **Framework:** TanStack Start (file-based routing via TanStack Router,
  `src/routes/`, generated route tree in `src/routeTree.gen.ts`) — **not
  Next.js.** No App Router, no `app/` directory, no `next.config.js`.
- **UI:** React 19, Tailwind CSS, Radix UI primitives (`src/components/ui/`)
- **Language:** TypeScript (strict mode — see `tsconfig.json`)
- **Build tool:** Vite
- **Validation:** Zod
- **Integration:** `@zapier/zapier-sdk` — the sole integration backbone;
  see `src/lib/zapier-dispatch.ts` and `src/lib/zapier-server.ts`
- **Package manager:** Bun (`bun.lock`, `bunfig.toml`) — use `bun`
  commands, not `npm`/`yarn`, in project tooling and docs
- **Testing:** **Planned: Vitest. Not installed yet** — there is
  currently no test runner and no test files in this repo. Do not
  reference `jest`, `jest.mock`, or `jest-environment-jsdom` in new code
  or docs; use Vitest's equivalents (`vi.fn`, `vi.spyOn`, `vi.mock`) once
  it's added.
- **Linting/formatting:** ESLint (flat config, `eslint.config.js`) +
  Prettier
- **Persistence:** **None for the original, non-Admin product.** No
  database, no Prisma, no PostgreSQL, no Redis there. **Superseded for the
  Admin capability:** a persistence layer for organization/user/role/session
  data is now planned; no technology is approved yet — see
  `docs/ADMIN_ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- **Auth:** The Zapier SDK credential (CLI login locally, or
  `ZAPIER_CREDENTIALS` for CI/prod) remains the only credential connecting
  the app to a Zapier account — unchanged for the original, non-Admin
  product. **Superseded for the Admin capability:** an application-level
  end-user login/session system is now planned separately; no approach
  selected yet — see `docs/ADMIN_ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- **Error/observability tooling:** Lovable's own utilities
  (`src/lib/error-capture.ts`, `src/lib/error-page.ts`,
  `src/lib/lovable-error-reporting.ts`). No Sentry, no Winston/Pino.

## Commands

- `bun install` — install dependencies
- `bun run dev` — start the dev server (`vite dev`)
- `bun run build` — production build
- `bun run build:dev` — development-mode build
- `bun run preview` — preview a production build
- `bun run lint` — run ESLint
- `bun run format` — run Prettier
- `bun run zapier:connect` — Zapier SDK connect helper script
- **Test command — not yet available.** Add once Vitest is installed; do
  not assume it exists before then.

## Project Structure

```plaintext
src/
├── routes/          # TanStack Router file-based routes (index.tsx = main app)
├── components/ui/   # Radix-based UI primitives
├── hooks/           # React hooks
├── lib/             # zapier-dispatch.ts, zapier-server.ts, error/logging utilities
├── routeTree.gen.ts # generated by @tanstack/router-plugin — do not hand-edit
├── router.tsx, server.ts, start.ts
└── styles.css
```

## File Conventions

- Components: PascalCase
- Utilities/libs: camelCase
- Test files (once Vitest exists): `*.test.ts`/`*.test.tsx` alongside the
  source file being tested
